ASM14A.IOFM.ASM
                  2: *53*
                  3: *
                  4: * NAME: PNCHB
                  5: *        PUNCH (A) IN OBJECT TAPE.
                  6: *
                  7: * INPUT:
                  8: *        ACCA     BYTE TO BE PUNCHED
                  9: *        BBPTR    NEXT FREE BYTE IN BINARY BUFFER
                 10: *        *BBPTR   CURRENT CHECKSUM.
                 11: *
                 12: * OUTPUT:
                 13: *        BBPTR    NEXT FREE BYTE IN BINARY BUFFER
                 14: *        *BBPTR   CURRENT CHECKSUM
                 15: *
  2749           16: PNCHB    ;LDX      BBPTR             GET POINTER TO NEXT BYTE,
2749 DEBE        17:          LDX      BBPTR
274B 8C3077      18:          CPX      #BBEND            END OF BUFFER?
274E 2602        19:          BNE      PNCH1             B/ NO:  JUST ADD BYTE.
2750 8D0E        20:          BSR      PNCHIT            ELSE PUNCH THE BUFFER
2752 16          21: PNCH1    TAB                        GET COPY OF BYTE,
2753 EB00        22:          ADDB     0,X               MAKE NEW CHECKSUM;
2755 A700        23:          STAA     0,X               SAVE THIS BYTE,
2757 08          24:          INX
2758 E700        25:          STAB     0,X
                 26:          ;INC      BBCNT             INCREMENT # OF BYTES IN THIS RECORD.
275A 7C00C0      27:          INC      BBCNT
275D DFBE        28:          STX      BBPTR             AND SAVE POINTER
275F 39          29: PNCHR    RTS                        GO AWAY.




ASM/6800 1.3H4: 275F ASM/6800 1.4       - - - I / O    S E C T I O N - - -
08/16/82 00:00:00; Page 295; Form 22    - - - P N C H I T - - -
ASM14A.IOFM.ASM
                  2: *53*
                  3: *
                  4: * NAME:  PNCHIT
                  5: *        PUNCHES ACCUMULATED BINARY RECORD, RESETS THE POINTERS.
                  6: *        SAVES A.
                  7: *
  2760            8: PNCHIT   EQU      *
2760 D654         9:          LDAB     PASS              ANYTHING TO DO, THIS PASS?
2762 2711        10:          BEQ      PNCSET
2764 D6BA        11:          LDAB     OPTF              BINARY WANTED?
2766 C504        12:          BITB     #OPT:BO
2768 270B        13:          BEQ      PNCSET            B/ NO:  RETURN.
276A 36          14:          PSHA
276B D6C0        15:          LDAB     BBCNT             ANYTHING TO PUNCH?
                 16:          ;CMPB    #2
276D C102        17:          CMPB     #2
276F 2305        18:          BLS      PNCSPC            B/ NO:  JUST RESET THE BUFFER.
                 19: 
2771 8D50        20:          BSR      OutputSDOSrecord
2773 2001        21:          BRA      PNCSPC
                 22: 
                 23: *
                 24: * SET UP BUFFER FOR NEXT TIME THRU.
2775 36          25: PNCSET   PSHA                       EXTERNAL ENTRY:  SAVE ACCA
  2776           26: PNCSPC   ;LDX      #BBST             INITIALIZE POINTER,
2776 CE3035      27:          LDX      #BBST
                 28:          ;CLR      0,X                  **      CHECKSUM,
2779 6F00        29:          CLR      0,X
                 30:          ;CLR      BBCNT                **      COUNT,
277B 7F00C0      31:          CLR      BBCNT
277E DFBE        32:          STX      BBPTR                **      POINTER.
2780 9696        33:          LDAA     PC                   **      PC (HIGH)
2782 8DCE        34:          BSR      PNCH1
2784 9697        35:          LDAA     PC+1                 **      PC (LOW)
2786 8DCA        36:          BSR      PNCH1
2788 32          37:          PULA                       RESTORE ACCA,
2789 39          38:          RTS                        AND EXIT.




ASM/6800 1.3H4: 2789 ASM/6800 1.4       - - - I / O    S E C T I O N - - -
