ASM/6800 1.3H4: 27C2 ASM/6800 1.4       - - - I / O    S E C T I O N - - -
08/16/82 00:00:00; Page 298; Form 24    - - -  O u t p u t   S D O S   R e c o r d  - - -
ASM14A.IOFM.ASM
                  2: *****************************************************************************
                  3: *
                  4: * Name:  OutputSDOSrecord
                  5: *
                  6: * Function:
                  7: *        Outputs the record that has been accumulated in BBST..BBEND into
                  8: *        the current SDOS-style load file.  Attempts to optimize the
                  9: *        alignment of the load records according to SDOS conventions.
                 10: *
                 11: * Changed:                          Preserved:
                 12: *        A B C X                         ***NONE***
                 13: *
                 14: * Input:
                 15: *        BBST [0..1]                Base address of this load record.
                 16: *
                 17: *        BBCNT                      B/ Number of bytes in binary buffer,
                 18: *                                      including the base address.
                 19: *
                 20: *        BBST [2..BBCNT-1]          Data bytes to be output.  If BBCNT=2,
                 21: *                                      this is a null record and is ignored.
                 22: *
                 23: *        Currec+R$VALID             B/ Flag, indicating (if non-zero) that
                 24: *                                      a record segment is open in the output
                 25: *                                      file.
                 26: *
                 27: *        Currec+R$FILEBASE          Q/ File position pointer.  If R$VALID is
                 28: *                                      true, then this is the base file address
                 29: *                                      of the first data byte in the current
                 30: *                                      record.  If R$VALID is false, this is
                 31: *                                      the file address of the first available
                 32: *                                      byte in the file.
                 33: *
                 34: *        Currec+R$BASE              W/ [Assuming R$VALID is true:]  Target
                 35: *                                      load address of the first data byte in
                 36: *                                      the currently open record of the output
                 37: *                                      file.
                 38: *
                 39: *        Currec+R$LEN               W/ [Assuming R$VALID is true:] Length of
                 40: *                                      the currently open record of the output
                 41: *                                      file.  If R$VALID is false, this MUST




ASM/6800 1.3H4: 27C2 ASM/6800 1.4       - - - I / O    S E C T I O N - - -
08/16/82 00:00:00; Page 299; Form 24    - - -  O u t p u t   S D O S   R e c o r d  - - -
ASM14A.IOFM.ASM
                 42: *                                      be zero.
                 43: *
                 44: *****************************************************************************
                 45: 
  27C3           46: OutputSDOSrecord  EQU *
                 47:          ;LDX     BBST              Copy target load address for this record
27C3 FE3035      48:          LDX      BBST
27C6 FF3080      49:          STX      NEWREC+R$BASE       to a safe/handy place.
27C9 96C0        50:          LDAA     BBCNT             Load the length of the record,
27CB 8002        51:          SUBA     #2                  remove crud counting PC at head of record,
27CD 273E        52:          BEQ      OutSDOS%            B/ Split if there's nothing to output.
                 53: ;                                        (Redundant check).
27CF B73083      54:          STAA     NEWREC+R$LEN+1    Save the count in a safe/handy place.
                 55:          ;CLR     NEWREC+R$LEN      Zap the high order byte.  It makes Terry
27D2 7F3082      56:          CLR      NEWREC+R$LEN
                 57:                                     ; happier if we do it here.
                 58: 
                 59: **** Check alignment conditions, and call AlignSDOSrecord if appropriate ****
27D5 8D37        60:          BSR      CheckSDOSalign    Sets CY if we should align.
27D7 2403        61:          BCC      OutSDOS$1           B/ No alignment, si vous plait.
                 62:          ;JSR     AlignSDOSrecord   Else, do the alignment.
27D9 BD2888      63:          JSR      AlignSDOSrecord
                 64: 
                 65: **** Leave room for record header, if necessary ****
  27DC           66: OutSDOS$1         EQU *
27DC B6308C      67:          LDAA     CURREC+R$VALID    Are we currently building a record?
27DF 2603        68:          BNE      OutSDOS$2           B/ yeah.... no need for header.
                 69:          ;JSR     PutRecordHdr      Otherwise, put the record header.
27E1 BD2872      70:          JSR      PutRecordHdr
                 71: 
                 72: **** Output the record segment ****
  27E4           73: OutSDOS$2         EQU *
                 74:          ;JSR     GetNewrecBase     Prepare to make a file position....
27E4 BD29D1      75:          JSR      GetNewrecBase
                 76:          ;JSR     FilePosition        X will return as pointer to 4-byte buffer.
27E7 BD2953      77:          JSR      FilePosition
27EA C603        78:          LDAB     #BO                 which has been filled w/ appropriate file
                 79:          ;JSR     POSITION$           address.
27EC BD0126      80:          JSR      POSITION$
                 81:          ;LDX     #BBST+2           Load base address of record,




ASM/6800 1.3H4: 27EF ASM/6800 1.4       - - - I / O    S E C T I O N - - -
